%[text] # Exercise 3 Solution: Adapt a Shared Detector Threshold to Each Pump
%[text] This solution calibrates one shared `iforest` detector to each pump by updating only the detector threshold from that pump's normal operating data. It then keeps `deepantAD` as an optional comparison point for the final deployment discussion.
workshopRoot = fileparts(which("setupWorkshop"));
moduleFolder = fullfile(workshopRoot,"Bonus-ThresholdTuning");
addpath(fullfile(moduleFolder,"HelperFiles"))
load(fullfile(moduleFolder,"Data","pumpFleetData.mat"))
load(fullfile(moduleFolder,"Checkpoints","trainedPumpDetectors.mat"))

sharedDetector = detectorIForest;
detectorName = "iforest";
selectedAssetNames = string(selectedTestAssets);

assetIdx = zeros(numel(selectedAssetNames),1);
for k = 1:numel(selectedAssetNames)
    assetIdx(k) = find(strcmp(assetNames,selectedTestAssets{k}));
end

disp("Evaluating selected pump assets:") %[output:839f3a3e]
disp(selectedAssetNames) %[output:8bde277e]
%%
%[text] ## Threshold Mechanism on `pump-2-9`
assetToInspect = "pump-2-9";
inspectionTestIdx = find(selectedAssetNames == assetToInspect);
inspectionTrainIdx = find(strcmp(assetNames,assetToInspect));

normalAssetData = trainData{inspectionTrainIdx};
testAssetData = testData{inspectionTestIdx};
testAssetLabels = logical(testLabels{inspectionTestIdx});

sharedThreshold = sharedDetector.Threshold %[output:5f4a40d8]
tunedDetector = updateDetector(sharedDetector,normalAssetData);
tunedThreshold = tunedDetector.Threshold %[output:360b0a3d]
sharedResult = detect(sharedDetector,testAssetData,Resolution="sample");
tunedResult = detect(tunedDetector,testAssetData,Resolution="sample");

sharedMetrics = timeSeriesAnomalyMetrics(sharedResult.Labels,testAssetLabels,Method="point-adjusted");
tunedMetrics = timeSeriesAnomalyMetrics(tunedResult.Labels,testAssetLabels,Method="point-adjusted");

singlePumpResults = table( ... %[output:group:18cbb63d] %[output:4b42429a]
    ["Shared"; "Tuned"], ... %[output:4b42429a]
    [sharedThreshold; tunedThreshold], ... %[output:4b42429a]
    [sharedMetrics.F1Score; tunedMetrics.F1Score], ... %[output:4b42429a]
    [sharedMetrics.Precision; tunedMetrics.Precision], ... %[output:4b42429a]
    [sharedMetrics.Recall; tunedMetrics.Recall], ... %[output:4b42429a]
    [sharedMetrics.FalsePositiveRate; tunedMetrics.FalsePositiveRate], ... %[output:4b42429a]
    VariableNames=["ThresholdStrategy","Threshold","F1Score","Precision","Recall","FalsePositiveRate"]) %[output:group:18cbb63d] %[output:4b42429a]
%[text] **Precision** = when detector says anomaly, how often is it right?
%[text] **Recall** = of all real anomaly events, how many did the detector catch?
%[text] **F1 score** = balance of precision and recall
%[text] **False positive rate** = how much normal behavior was incorrectly flagged as anomalous?
plotThresholdMechanism(sharedDetector,normalAssetData,testAssetData,testAssetLabels,assetToInspect,detectorName) %[output:4f1ea6a0]
%%
%[text] ## Fleet Threshold Calibration
%[text] Apply this calibration to other pumps.
fleetResults = evaluateThresholdTuning(sharedDetector,trainData,assetIdx,testData,testLabels, ... %[output:group:389f9016] %[output:5de6a849]
    selectedAssetNames) %[output:group:389f9016] %[output:5de6a849]
%%
%[text] ## Optional Checkpoint: Compare with `deepantAD`
%[text] DeepantAD is a heavier-weight detector (neural network backbone). 
optionalDetectors = {detectorDeepAnt, detectorIForest};
optionalDetectorNames = ["deepantAD","iforest"];

[optionalMetricsTable,optionalComparison,optionalDetectorSummary, ...
    bestAbsoluteDetector,mostImprovedByTuning] = compareDetectorThresholdTuning( ...
    optionalDetectors,trainData,assetIdx,testData,testLabels, ...
    selectedAssetNames,optionalDetectorNames);

plotF1Comparison(optionalMetricsTable) %[output:4e421c46]
optionalComparison %[output:10c2a219]
optionalDetectorSummary %[output:67d888e8]
bestAbsoluteDetector %[output:92f916cd]
mostImprovedByTuning %[output:96b11a39]
%%
%[text] ## Interpretation
%[text] The direct `iforest` workflow shows how `updateDetector` moves the threshold for each pump and improves event-level detection. The optional comparison supports the final deployment discussion: `deepantAD` can remain the strongest absolute detector, while `iforest` can be the simpler detector that benefits most from calibration.

